-- challenge chal_coding_bjm_122 (mini_coding)
INSERT INTO challenge.challenges (public_id, course_id, module_id, lesson_id, name, title, description, status, difficulty, type, points, is_published, is_deleted)
VALUES ('chal_coding_bjm_122', (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'background-jobs-messaging'), (SELECT id FROM course.module WHERE course_id = (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'background-jobs-messaging') AND order_index = 1 AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), (SELECT id FROM course.lesson WHERE content_source = 'lesson-bjm-1-2' AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), 'job-state-machine', 'A job state machine that rejects what cannot happen', 'Every CodeDev background job (grade a submission, send a certificate email, recompute the leaderboard, generate a course export) has a state that only changes through events. Write applyEvent(jobs, event, maxAttempts): apply ONE event to the jobs map; if it is accepted, update the job and return null; if it is rejected, change nothing and return the reason. States: queued, running, succeeded, failed, cancelled, retrying. Checks, in this order (the first failing check gives the reason): 1. event.type is not one of enqueue, start, heartbeat, succeed, fail, timeout, cancel, retry-scheduled -> "unknown event type". 2. a fail event whose failure is not "retryable" or "permanent" -> "invalid failure kind". 3. enqueue of an existing job id -> "job already exists" (otherwise create the job: queued, attempts 0, workerId null, lastFailure null). 4. any other event for a job id that does not exist -> "unknown job". 5. the event is not allowed in the job''s state -> "<type> not allowed when <state>" (for example "succeed not allowed when queued"); allowed: start from queued or retrying; heartbeat, succeed, fail and timeout from running; cancel from queued, running or retrying; retry-scheduled from failed. 6. heartbeat, succeed or fail from a workerId that is not the job''s workerId -> "stale worker <workerId> (owner <job.workerId>)". 7. retry-scheduled when the last failure was permanent -> "permanent failure"; retry-scheduled when attempts >= maxAttempts -> "max attempts reached". Effects: start -> running, attempts + 1, workerId = event.workerId, lastFailure null; heartbeat -> no change; succeed -> succeeded, workerId null; fail -> failed, lastFailure = event.failure, workerId null; timeout -> failed, lastFailure "retryable", workerId null; cancel -> cancelled, workerId null; retry-scheduled -> retrying. Input (JSON on stdin): { maxAttempts, events }. The runner prints one line per rejected event ("rejected #<1-based position> <type> <jobId>: <reason>"), then every job in the order it was enqueued ("<id> <state> attempts=<n>"). Up to about 1,100 events.', 'open', 'medium'::difficulty_question, 'mini_coding', 30, true, false)
