14:02:41.611 certificates-worker-3 job=8812 attempt=2 issue-certificate user=u_anna course=redis-patterns
14:02:41.690 certificates-worker-3 job=8812 INSERT certificates serial=C-5522 OK
14:02:41.702 certificates-worker-3 job=8812 completed

Statement: "The queue broke its delivery guarantee here: job 8812 should not have been delivered again, because worker 7 had already written the certificate."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The queue only learns that a job is done from the acknowledgement, and worker 7 was killed after its INSERT but before process() returned, so no ack was ever sent. From the queue''s side the job was received and abandoned, and delivering it again after the timeout is exactly what at-least-once delivery promises: without it, the crash would have lost the certificate instead of duplicating it. The fix belongs in the worker: an idempotency key claimed in the same transaction as the insert, so the second delivery finds the key and does nothing. The misconception is that a queue can know about side effects it was never told about; no queue can offer exactly-once delivery end to end, only at-least-once delivery that a worker turns into an exactly-once effect.', 1, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_bjm_211') AND order_index = 1)
    RETURNING id
)
