Statement: "Since 09:02 no submission other than sub_8812 has been attempted: every attempt in the logs is for the same job id, and nothing has been graded since then."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. Every attempt line in B names job=sub_8812, with the attempt counter going from 1 to 360 at one attempt every 30 s (3 hours = 10,800 s / 30 s = 360), and A shows 0 graded per minute from 09:05 while the waiting count rises. The other replicas only log that the group is locked. Reading the evidence means noticing what is absent too: no other job id appears at all. The common mistake is to read "80,000 waiting" as "the workers are busy with 80,000 jobs" when they are stuck on one.', 1, 5
