Statement: "The step from 2 to 6 grader workers at 10:15 was too small: the queue keeps growing because 6 workers cannot keep up with 445 submissions a minute."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. A shows no change at all after 10:15: graded/min stays at 0 and waiting keeps growing by the same amount every half hour. B says why: grader-worker-2d11 is idle because the message group "grading" is locked by an in-flight message. With one group and concurrency 1 per group, only one message can be in flight at a time however many workers run, and that message is sub_8812. Before 09:02 two workers graded about 600 per minute, more than the arrival rate. The misconception is that a growing queue always means too little capacity; here the capacity is idle.', 3, 5
