Statement: "Wrapping the send and setEmailStatus in one database transaction fixes this: if the worker dies before the commit, the transaction rolls back and nothing has happened."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. A database transaction can only roll back what the database did. The email left through the provider''s API at 10:14:02.118, before the process died; rolling back the status update leaves it at pending, which is exactly the state that made worker c07 send again. Wrapping the send in a transaction even makes things slightly worse: the transaction stays open during a network call. The misconception is that a transaction makes any block of code atomic; side effects outside the database need their own protection: an idempotency key the provider honours, or a marker written before the side effect with a rule for what to do when the marker is found.', 1, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_bjm_331') AND order_index = 1)
    RETURNING id
)
